{"name":"Spores","hex":"#7f8162","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Spores","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Spores"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spore","blocks":[{"text":"In biology, a spore is a unit of sexual or asexual reproduction that may be adapted for dispersal and for survival, often for extended periods of time, in unfavourable conditions. Spores form part of the life cycles of many plants, algae, fungi and protozoa. They were thought to have appeared as early as the mid-late Ordovician period as an adaptation of early land plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Sporic_meiosis.svg/330px-Sporic_meiosis.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spore","wikidata":"Q177332"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Brachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg/500px-Brachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Brachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg/1280px-Brachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Brachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg/500px-Brachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh snow partially covers rough-stalked feather-moss (Brachythecium rutabulum), growing on a thinned hybrid black poplar (Populus x canadensis). The last stage of the moss lifecycle is shown, where the sporophytes are visible before dispersion of their spores: the calyptra (1) is still attached to the capsule (3). The tops of the gametophytes (2) can be discerned as well. Inset shows the surrounding, black poplars growing on sandy loam on the bank of a kolk, with the detail area marked.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrachythecium_rutabulum_on_Populus_x_canadensis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Sporangium_of_fungi.jpg/500px-Sporangium_of_fungi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Sporangium_of_fungi.jpg/1280px-Sporangium_of_fungi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Sporangium_of_fungi.jpg/500px-Sporangium_of_fungi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sporangium of Fungi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASporangium_of_fungi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Rhizopus_zygospores.jpg/500px-Rhizopus_zygospores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Rhizopus_zygospores.jpg/500px-Rhizopus_zygospores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zygospores on Rhizopus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhizopus_zygospores.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Bitunicate_ascus_and_ascospores_of_Didymella_rabiei.png/330px-Bitunicate_ascus_and_ascospores_of_Didymella_rabiei.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Bitunicate_ascus_and_ascospores_of_Didymella_rabiei.png/330px-Bitunicate_ascus_and_ascospores_of_Didymella_rabiei.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ascospores of Didymella Rabiei","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%